    "body": "The `rtp_receive_packet` function (via `fill_data_into_slot`) relied on the `data_length_full` field in the RTP header to allocate the frame buffer, but failed to verify that the actual payload length of the incoming packet fit within this allocated size. A malicious peer could send a packet with a small `data_length_full` but a large payload, causing `memcpy` to write past the end of the buffer.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds a bounds check to ensure that the packet offset plus the payload length does not exceed the total frame length. Tested via unit tests.\r\n\r\n<!-- Reviewable:start -->\r\n- - -\r\nThis change is [<img src=\"https://reviewable.io/review_button.svg\" height=\"34\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"Reviewable\"/>](https://reviewable.io/reviews/TokTok/c-toxcore/2939)\r\n<!-- Reviewable:end -->\r\n",
